#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0815-A expect=violation domain=ADPPK
#note "PRESENCE SISTER (minted by Fix #331 under M2-D24 bucket 3, owner ruling 2026-08-22; sheet issue owed for the missing sheet entry). ADPPK (declared subclass POPULATION PHARMACOKINETIC ANALYSIS) carries SUBJID but NO SUBJIDN column at all. The Check is a pure var_exists combination, so it folds at dataset level and the finding is reported ONCE although both rows carry SUBJID; the value rule CDISC-AD0815 takes an auditable SKIP on the same data (its Requirements.Variables.All now names both SUBJID and SUBJIDN). The sister is SCOPED to the popPK subclass (review S1): USUBJIDN/SUBJIDN/SITEIDN exist only in ADPPKIG, so without that gate it would fire on every plain BDS dataset -- see -valid_plain_bds-ADLBC. If this reports 2, the broadcast fold has stopped applying to exists-only Checks -- escalate."
#expectViolationCount 1
# Declared-tier scope: structure=/subclass= state the ADaM data structure and the popPK subclass this
# minimal table stands for; #define is their mandatory carrier (ScenarioDeclaredScopeProvider.install).
#define standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADPPK structure=BDS subclass=POPPK
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col SUBJID type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 1015
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | 1023
---
